Subject: [PATCH v4 2/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Leave the header check to
 OpenSMTPD
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: zmspquwwwtqkwzxtrykkkkuqywvnpluy
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:51:47 +0000

The spec has OpenSMTPD refuse a post with a broken header, or without
exactly one From, Subject, and Message-ID. OpenSMTPD does part of that
on its own. Its parser refuses a header line it cannot read with a 550
before the queue. On a loopback listener it gives a Message-ID and a
Date to a message that lacks them. Checking the rest would take a
filter of our own in every SMTP session, to refuse faults that do not
stop the list from being threaded.

- The spec asks only for what OpenSMTPD does itself.
- Acceptance step 6 posts a broken header, and a message with no
  Message-ID that should land with one.
